fact WorkItem(id: "WI-301", description: some(value: "Effect-set type representation: make `Effect = {}` and `Effect = {Modify[s]}` expressible as a type-argument value, end to end. PROBLEM: an effect set has no representation as a type-binding value. (1) GRAMMAR — sort_binding's value slot is `_type` = {simple_type, parameterized_type, variable_term, tuple_type, arrow_type} (tree-sitter-anthill/grammar.js:1001); the effect-set form `_effect_set` (grammar.js:369) lives only in `effects` clauses and arrow `@`, and its braced variant is commaSep1, so empty `{}` has NO production anywhere. Thus `Effect = {}` / `Effect = {Modify[s]}` are ungrammatical in both named and positional instantiation forms. (2) TYPE MODEL — stdlib/anthill/prelude/sort.anthill's Type enum carries effects only inside arrow(param, result, effects: List[Type]); a TypeBinding(param, value: Type) cannot hold a set of effects. (3) REFLECTION/SPEC — stdlib/anthill/reflect/typing.anthill + docs/proposals/typing_pass_spec.anthill treat effects as List[Type] on arrows only (effects_subset / merge_effects / external_effects), never as a type-argument value; stdlib/anthill/prelude/function.anthill:15 explicitly flags 'exact encoding depends on how empty effect sets are represented'. DESIGN (agreed): add `entity effect_set(effects: List[Type])` to the Type enum, mirroring arrow's effects: List[Type]; `{}` -> effect_set(effects: []), `{Modify[s]}` -> effect_set(effects: [Modify[s]]); this also fixes the pure-Function `E = {}` encoding. TASK: (a) grammar — let an effect-set expression (incl. empty `{}`) be used where a `_type` is expected (the sort_binding value slot), regenerate parser, add corpus tests; (b) converter — build effect_set Type terms from the new node; (c) prelude/sort.anthill — add the effect_set Type constructor; (d) reflect/typing.anthill + typing_pass_spec.anthill — type/classify effect-set type arguments; (e) restore explicit `Effect = {}` on the 3 list.anthill facts (Collection / IndexedSeq / Iteration) that the substrate change temporarily dropped. ACCEPTANCE: `fact Iteration[Iterator = List[T], Element = T, Effect = {}]` parses and stores an effect_set binding (not silently dropped); a reflection query over List's Iteration provides-fact sees Effect = effect_set([]); typer accepts effect-set type arguments; cargo-test green. SCOPE: converter + typer are Rust-only (scaland has no typer); the grammar change is shared. CONTEXT: surfaced while checking whether `fact Iteration[List[T], T, {}]` (positional) equals the named form — positional type args DO work (loader maps index -> declared param via type_params_of_sort), but the `{}` effect arg never parsed; the silent drop only became visible once parse() started surfacing tree-sitter ERROR/MISSING nodes (the WI-303 substrate). RELATED (separate, not in scope): fully-qualified names are rejected as instantiation_term functors (reflect.anthill `fact anthill.prelude.Modifiable[T = KB]` had to be rewritten to the imported short name `fact Modifiable[T = KB]`) — file its own WI if dotted instantiation functors should be supported."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Rejected(reason: "Superseded by proposal 045 / WI-320 (delivered): effect-sets are NOT type arguments. The agreed `entity effect_set(effects: List[Type])` design no longer exists — replaced by the structural `EffectsRows(EffectExpression)` Type form + the EffectsRuntime row-variable model (`effects E` sugar -> `sort E = ? requires EffectsRuntime[Effects = E]` + loader auto-requires). 045 §788 records this reframing. The concrete gap WI-301 named — a closed `{}` effect on a pure provider fact — is resolved by DERIVATION, not by a writable type-argument: the typer grounds the spec-op's declared `effects E` to the carrier's effect at the consumption boundary (pure provider => {}). That grounding is WI-357 (concrete carrier, delivered; effect-close at typing.rs:3115-3120) and WI-365 (abstract self-receiver dual). Under this model List's provider facts CORRECTLY leave Effect unbound; the stale `pending WI-301` comments in list.anthill were re-pointed at the 045 row model. No grammar widening for an effect-set in type-argument position is pursued.", at: "2026-06-02T17:43:07Z"))
